<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- Automatic cookie renewal, The Stage only for now (BRO-4183).

         Every 6h: scripts/renew-cookies.js probes a walled Stage review
         (free, plain HTTPS from this residential IP, same probe as
         check-cookie-health.yml Layer 3). Logged in: exits in seconds.
         Logged out: reuses the persistent profile's session if it is still
         alive, else logs in ONCE (password from the macOS Keychain), pushes
         COOKIES_BUNDLE_* via extract-safari-cookies.py (from-local mode), and
         confirms with a live check-cookie-health run. CAPTCHA, emailed
         code, rejected password, or 2 logins in 7 days: stops, emails one
         link, and stays stopped. Recover with
         renew-cookies.js in manual mode (see its header for flags) (you log in
         inside the same profile, so no extra device), or its reset flag after
         fixing the cause some other way. Probe pages that aren't the known
         registration gate (Cloudflare challenge, maintenance) never trigger
         a login.

         MAC STUDIO ONLY. Never add Stage login to CI: per-runner logins
         tripped the 2-device limit on 2026-03-30.

         Do NOT install before the first supervised run:
           security add-generic-password, service broadwayscorecard-cookie-renew, account thestage-email, value = your Stage login email
           security add-generic-password, service broadwayscorecard-cookie-renew, account thestage-password, prompt for password
           (exact commands: scripts/lib/cookie-renew.js readKeychain docstring)
           node scripts/renew-cookies.js (outlet thestage, headed flag; exact flags in its header)
         then confirm The Stage's account page shows a single active session.

         .env is sourced for RESEND_API_KEY/OWNER_EMAIL (alert email) only;
         launchd does not inherit shell env. `gh` must be authenticated with
         secrets:write on thomaspryor/Broadwayscore. The first Keychain read
         from launchd may show an "allow access" prompt: choose Always Allow.

         Install:  cp scripts/launchd/com.broadwayscore.cookie-renew.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
                   launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.broadwayscore.cookie-renew.plist
         Manual run: launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.cookie-renew
         Kill:     launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/com.broadwayscore.cookie-renew -->
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.broadwayscore.cookie-renew</string>
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>/bin/bash</string>
        <string>-lc</string>
        <string>cd /Users/tompryor/Broadwayscore &amp;&amp; set -a &amp;&amp; source .env &amp;&amp; set +a &amp;&amp; exec node scripts/renew-cookies.js --outlet=thestage</string>
    </array>
    <key>StartInterval</key>
    <integer>21600</integer>
    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/cookie-renew.log</string>
    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>/tmp/cookie-renew.log</string>
    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>
</dict>
</plist>
